WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.860
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.870
Episode 11

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.870
It was as the White Snow

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.660
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.630
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.720
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.840
Your answers will...

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.850
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.260
Even more...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.140
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:46.350
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:53.360
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.910
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.040
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.000
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.220
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.480
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
The seasons have passed, and it's already winter!!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
This time, it's an inter-school camp with Takami Girls' School

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
The President is staying home to study for exams.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
Kawamura Akina and Minami Sayuri have already been accepted.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.120
It’s freezing.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:45.870
No!

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.710
This is beyond freezing; it burns!

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.130
Who said the winter was warm this year?!

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.630
Didn’t I warn you?

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.130
You need to wear three times as many layers.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.470
Souma-sensei, that’s not fair!

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.800
Yay, snow!

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.260
Is she serious?

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.220
I’m... I’m shivering down to my bones.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.810
No, stop!

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.020
Please stop blowing, wind!

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.650
Where’s everyone from Takami School?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.940
They took the express train before ours, so...

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.400
Hey!

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.700
Souei-san!

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.620
Hey, Souei High School!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.540
You dressed lightly!!

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.700
You didn’t!!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.000
This is how it should be.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.670
What are you saying when you look so cold?

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.840
<i>The Astronomy Club is staying for three nights in Nagashiratsuru. </i>

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:37.840
Sorry about this...

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.880
We took winter too lightly.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:44.470
Geez, and I even gave you a paper with what to bring on it.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.930
Didn’t you read it?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.770
Well, I did, but...

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.980
I couldn’t tell whether or not you were serious.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.940
I was completely serious!!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.690
But she wasn’t wearing any pants...

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.530
She has fur!

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.990
What we must first fight... is the coldness.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.570
The cold air will creep into even the slightest crack.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.080
Only after you endure it can you do activities in the cold.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.170
Hoshimi-chan and Yaraicchi certainly meet the standards.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.000
Ooyagi-kun and Edogawa-kun, you need more layers!

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:15.420
And finally...

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.050
It’s not like... I wasn’t thinking at all...

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.390
You may as well be nude out here in those skinny jeans.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.720
Allow us to demonstrate proper winter armor!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:25.680
Underwear:

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.470
Wear something like polyester that absorbs moisture and dries quickly.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.060
Fleece:

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.020
Wear something that insulates well like a fleece or a sweater.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:33.980
Outerwear:

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.980
Material that blocks the wind. Overalls are extremely good insulators as well.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:42.820
You can put on hats, pocket heaters, and various other options to adjust to your liking.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.660
Good thing I brought extra clothes just in case.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.490
I think I’ll wear steteco.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.950
I-I’ll be fine.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.420
I also brought extra clothing.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.000
I just thought it’d be hotter in the day.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.000
Really?

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.090
Then all is well, I guess.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.470
Now then, it’s great to have you here.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.510
If you need anything, just ask us.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.140
After all, we’re going to be eating and sleeping together for three nights.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.100
Not again.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.020
These glasses are so loose.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.600
<i>So... hot. </i>

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.520
Come on, guys.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.650
Ann, you’re the new President.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.270
Get a hold of yourself.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.520
N-Nice to meet you.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.610
Come on!

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.190
You know some of them from HSAN.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.070
Don’t be so―

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.110
It’s quite all right.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.660
I’m sure the ladies are just nervous.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.080
To tell you the truth, my heart is racing as if the bells of―

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.330
He’s the...

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.670
Please! Let me photograph a girl!

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.010
Huh...?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.180
Wow!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.350
Is the sky clearer?

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.520
The weather changes rapidly here.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.060
It’s amazing.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.820
It hasn’t even snowed in Kosugino City.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.530
It’s been ages since I was surrounded by this much snow.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.200
By the way, Mihoshi,

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.620
I’d think you’ve been to a lot of places, but you get excited so easily.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.120
My dad took me to all sorts of places when he was alive.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.200
Not so much, now.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.210
That’s why.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.460
That’s right.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.500
Sorry.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.210
Jeez!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.250
Stop apologizing about it!

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.170
What could this be?

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.090
Love, perhaps?

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.220
Very nice.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.630
Don’t mind us!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:25.630
You’ve got it all wrong!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.800
But aren’t co-ed schools full of couples?

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.140
Is that how you see it?!

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.640
You know, I have to hand it to you, Sakai-sensei.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.140
Procuring a place for winter camp completely slipped my mind.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.270
Oh, no.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.690
It’s a pleasure to be able to accompany you.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.610
This is your first time in a winter camp, right?

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.740
As the Astronomy Club, yes.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:51.280
But we’ve already seen quite a lot of winter constellations.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:56.580
Orion, Pleiades, Winter Triangle, and Winter Hexagon.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Not to worry.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.050
You’ve only seen them from the city, right?

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.340
Don’t worry.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:06.720
You’ll be way more mesmerized.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.430
Isn’t that right, Hoshimi-chan?

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.430
Yeah.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.010
I’m so excited!

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.470
In any case, do you think Orion is a hot teen?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.560
Or could he be a hairy hunter?

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.060
I prefer the teen, since he dresses like this.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:20.230
What’re you saying?

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.650
The old man is so much better!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.110
The beard?

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:22.860
Is that your fetish?

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:23.650
You don’t get it?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:26.400
We’re here!

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:28.360
Hello and welcome.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.450
It’s great to be here this year as well.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.370
Oh my God!

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.830
It’s an observatory!

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:34.160
Yep.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.540
Wow!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.750
I can even see my own breath in here!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.170
My apologies.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.090
The heater’s malfunctioning.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.550
It happens every year, and it gets fixed right away.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:47.800
The kitchen’s this way.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.260
We’ll all be cooking together later.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.550
Now, let’s go check each of our rooms.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:53.930
Okay!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.890
Here, let me take it.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.230
It’s actually pretty heavy.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:04.940
I can carry it by myself.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.820
The boys’ rooms are over there, right?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.190
What’s in it?

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.200
I’m not telling.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.780
Well, see ya, Saku-chan.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:13.570
Okay.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.040
Hime-chan, are you okay?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:18.960
I’m fine.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.250
Do you want this?!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.120
There’s a pocket heater, too!

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.290
I am fine!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.840
I’m perfectly fine!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.060
I can’t feel my feet.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:42.060
I’ve never played so much in the snow before.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:42.940
Yeah, well...

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.270
Make sure to get changed.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:45.520
You could catch a cold.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:50.190
I had no idea... that high school girls did such things.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.780
I... I...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.410
Edogawa?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.790
I want to get as many photos of it as possible!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:58.580
Hey...

00:07:58.790 --> 00:07:59.500
Minami-san!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:00.960
Akira-san!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.540
Oh, you wanna help?

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.170
You the man!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.210
What?

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.340
If you have to ask...

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:10.170
We’re building something.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.050
You know, you could get a serious frostbite like that.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:18.890
By the way...

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.310
what’s our main focus in stargazing here?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.060
Usually, we have the camp after the year ends

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.900
and watch the Quadrantids, but...

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.940
The weather in January didn’t look good, so we moved it up.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.570
So I guess just having fun watching stars and taking photographs.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:38.870
It’ll be our last camp, so I hope it’ll be a blast.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.580
Though... it can’t start with this weather...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.840
The weather is all part of enjoying the camp.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:56.760
<i>I picked these clothes out, so I can’t complain.</i>

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.850
I need to find something I can wear in layers.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:04.770
These tights... and I can wear pajama pants underneath...

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.360
<i>It doesn’t work!</i>

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.440
<i>I just thought it’d be cute in the snow.</i>

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:19.950
<i>I did see a convenience store of some sort on the way here.</i>

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.500
<i>They may not have clothes, but maybe they’ll have underwear.</i>

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.210
Firstly, keep your fingers and toes warm!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:33.510
Secondly, carry your own flashlight at all times.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:37.220
Thirdly, before you leave, let someone know where you’re going!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.260
Okay, we get it.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.970
Let’s play some games.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.310
It’s great to have veterans here.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.060
Yeah!

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:50.730
<i>Hime-chan?</i>

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.320
And now, for the weather report.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.110
Cold air has rapidly risen to high altitudes

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:01.660
and will most likely bring a strong blizzard to the Nagashiratsuru area.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.080
Please be careful.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.370
<i>Nagashiratsuru area?</i>

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.250
<i>No...</i>

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:18.380
<i>I thought... all convenient stores were open twenty-four-seven!</i>

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:28.940
Missing?

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.310
Makita-san?

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.610
And... Mihoshi said she saw her leave.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.190
What should we do?

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:40.320
Why did she go out alone at night?

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.450
Wasn’t she listening to us?

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.240
That’s right!

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:44.490
She wasn’t here!

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.950
She couldn’t have heard you!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.370
How did this happen...?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.460
All because I had trouble fixing the heater...

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.250
Makita...

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.040
What should I do?

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:55.000
She could die out there in this freezing blizzard.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.130
Let’s calm down.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.090
Let’s check if she’s back first.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:10:59.720
Say...

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.220
She... brought extra clothing... didn’t she?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:09.600
Mihoshi!

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.270
When you saw her, how was she―

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:13.560
Mihoshi?

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.580
<i>It’s white.</i>

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.250
<i>What am I supposed to do at a time like this?</i>

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.250
<i>Dig a hole?</i>

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.920
<i>I can’t do it!</i>

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.260
<i>I’ll just keep walking.</i>

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.300
<i>I just need to walk back to where everyone is.</i>

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:42.800
<i>It’ll be all right.</i>

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:43.640
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.600
<i>Just follow your own footprints.</i>

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.520
<i>Your own...</i>

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.690
I can’t take this!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.740
I can’t tell right from left!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:05.280
You dummy!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:06.490
You dummy!

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.080
Hime, you dummy!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.000
Guys... Teacher...

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:16.210
Ooyagi-kun!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.550
Makita-san!

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:20.670
Hime-chan!

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:21.880
Mihoshi!

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.180
Guys, make sure you don’t go out too far!

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:24.930
Got it!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.350
It’s getting even heavier.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.220
I can’t see anything.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.430
Wherever and whenever I am...

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:31.430
Hey!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.640
What, is it my turn?!

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.400
And why is the window open?

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.560
This is not the time to be sleeping!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.520
What are you saying?!

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.980
Do you know how hard I worked this afternoon?!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.900
I dug and tossed, and dug and tossed impossible amounts of snow to build those things!

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.360
Can’t I rest a litt―

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:46.450
That’s not what I mean!

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:47.620
She’s missing!

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:48.620
Makita-san’s missing!

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.950
And we think Mihoshi may have gone after her.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.460
That’s terrible!

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:56.790
That’s what I’ve been saying!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:01.170
I contacted the fire station, but since it’s a blizzard out...

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:04.260
I hope they’ve at least found each other.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.930
I’ve received an update regarding the blizzard warning.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.640
Nagashiratsuru area...

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:12.810
No!

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.850
Girls, let’s settle down.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:19.690
Do you think that they’ve... gone into the woods to take a picture somewhere?

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.820
I’d say they most likely didn’t.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.690
Let’s keep searching in this direction.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:27.660
Maybe she went to find something she lost or wanted to go into town.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:29.990
This happens every now and then, you know.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.160
I don’t know what you mean.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.330
At any rate, we are here.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.000
That’s where we played, and that’s just a giant field of snow.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.050
They must’ve lost their way in this blizzard.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.210
Hime-hime!

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.720
Mihoshi-senpai!

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.600
<i>I... can’t...</i>

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.980
<i>Where... am I?</i>

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.780
<i>Am I... going to die?</i>

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.030
<i>It’s so cold.</i>

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:06.820
<i>Guys...</i>

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.570
<i>Ooyagi-kun...</i>

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.450
Makita-san!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.500
Makita-san!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.000
Makita-san!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.920
Thank God you woke up.

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.390
You’re so stupid, freezing up like this.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.430
Do you know how worried I was?

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:32.890
I’m sorry...

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.020
I’m sorry, Ooyagi―

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:40.690
No!

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.270
No!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.730
I don’t want to say goodbye now!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.700
I definitely don’t!

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:53.410
I’m still young, and I want to dress up more!

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.790
I haven’t even confessed... let alone kissed yet!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.090
I’m just... getting started in life!

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.970
<i>I feel so weak.</i>

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.890
<i>Maybe God’s punishing me.</i>

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:24.270
<i>Because I’m always feeling jealous, and I’m dishonest...</i>

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:28.070
Hime.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.360
Hime.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.910
<i>Papa... Mama... Sis...</i>

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.370
Hey, you Drift!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.370
Tell me, Drift!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.250
Stop calling me Drift!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.670
Drift!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.580
Is that natural curl?

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.210
How many times do I need to tell you?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.250
<i>Shoot...</i>

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.670
<i>This isn’t looking very good.</i>

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.340
Wait, please don’t go!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.640
No, it’s all right.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.810
You have such nice hair, after all.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.140
<i>Ooyagi-kun...</i>

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.400
<i>Guys...</i>

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:06.860
<i>I’m sorry...</i>

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.280
<i>Kuma-tan...</i>

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:14.910
Kuma-tan?

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.990
Hey, wait!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.660
What the hell’s with this carefree art?!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.210
Hot Kuma-tan Pocket Heater?!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.120
What the hell is this?!

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.290
I did <i>not</i> bring this with me!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:27.960
Back then...

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:39.850
Old-... Mihoshi-senpai...

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.810
You rang?!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:49.820
Hime-chan...

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.440
Thank God.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.610
I saw you leave by yourself, and you didn’t come back.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.660
I thought you got lost, so...

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.240
Hey..

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:00.370
What are you doing looking like that...?

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.210
Why did you come for me...?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.750
There, all better.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:12.710
Here.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.300
Wait, your warm-ups?

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:15.930
Now, follow me!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.050
Let’s go back to where everyone is.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:18.930
Okay.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:20.560
What was that sound?

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:31.570
Souma-sensei!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:32.530
No luck.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.030
I couldn’t see a thing.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.410
She wasn’t at the bus stop either, so they’re probably...

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:40.330
Teacher, please let us go search for her too!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.370
I know how you feel, but it’d be too dangerous.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.120
But!

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.160
Please, we also feel the same!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.000
Ann...

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:47.870
Please!

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:49.210
We won’t stay out for too long.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:52.880
Hime-hime!

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:55.090
Mihoshi-senpai!

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.470
See the light!

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.890
Thank you, Hime-chan... for pulling me out.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.850
Just barely!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:09.060
You could’ve died if you didn’t hand me the light first!

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:11.480
And now we have no idea where to go...

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.360
Don’t worry.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:13.650
We can figure it out if the sky clears up.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.990
As if that’s going to happen any time soon!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.570
But thank goodness we found this little snow cave.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.240
What did you come here to do anyway?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.620
Though I shouldn’t be complaining since you saved me...

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.540
Here. Chocolates.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:26.710
They’re good.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:27.750
Are you even listening?!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.500
The chocolate was good.

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.170
You know...

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:36.550
I know how you feel.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:41.760
Back when I was little, I sneaked out in the snow and got scolded for it.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.850
I thought I could see the stars if I went to a place that wasn’t snowing.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:51.400
It was really cold and lonely, but the stars after the blizzard were extremely pretty.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.270
But you can’t sneak out anymore.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.690
If someone didn’t come back, it’d be too sad.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.320
I’m... sorry...

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.240
But... it’s not fair, Senpai.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.000
Why are you always high above the clouds?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.000
Rising and rising and rising and rising, all the time,

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.250
while I’m down here, overcome with jealousy.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.010
I feel so stupid.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.550
Back at the hall, I was actually happy when you looked out for me,

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:29.980
but I was just too stubborn and... look where that got me.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:36.020
<i>If you were a cloud, I would be the snow.</i>

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:40.150
<i>Piling up, and getting hard.</i>

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.160
I know I shouldn’t be saying this right now,

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.580
but Senpai, please acknowledge me more!

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.420
If you won’t accept me as your rival, I...

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:00.880
Sure.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:01.970
All right.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.680
But I won’t lose either.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.140
<i>Her eyes are different...</i>

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.470
<i>They’re looking straight at me.</i>

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:12.890
<i>But... I love Ooyagi-kun just as much as you do.</i>

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:14.020
Okay.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:17.480
Shh.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:19.320
Can you hear the wind?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:38.210
Aldebaran, Rigel, Capella, Pollux, Betelgeuse, and Procyon.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.590
Sirius...

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:42.340
Senpai... what is this?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.930
I can’t connect them in such a dense cluster.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.810
Light... arrows?

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:58.730
Fire!

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:02.110
If you’ve lost your way, please find it.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:09.240
You’re kidding!

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.290
Goodness...

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.080
There’s a limit to how reckless you can be!

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.420
Totally!

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.670
I thought I told you to ask me!

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.130
I-I’m sorry.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.380
I have tons of clothes you can use!

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:25.510
Look.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.090
You’ve even made Yaraicchi cry.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.390
But I’m truly glad that you both made it back just fine.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.310
Yes, yes.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.520
We found them.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.230
The sky’s cleared up as well.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:37.520
You worried me, too.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:38.940
Ooyagi-kun...

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.610
The heater’s working again!

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:42.570
Finally...

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.240
Finally, I feel warm.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.660
All right, then shall we get ready for the real thing?

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:48.280
Yes!

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.120
Really?

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:49.950
Hime-chan.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:50.700
Yes?

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:56.040
I-I-I know I said some things earlier, but that was just ’cause my head was a little...

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:56.790
Well...

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.960
Is it in who can stay outside and watch the stars the longest?

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:03.590
Or is it in who can find the best stargazing spot?

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:07.630
Rival! Rival!

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:12.970
What... What in the world did you think I was talking about?!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.780
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.450
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.740
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.920
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.500
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.880
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.180
playing with my memories

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.020
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:02.980
Into the future,

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:11.530
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.950
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:21.040
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.140
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:40.390
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:49.690
Final episode of Sora no Manimani: Star Sky Loop.
